+## IRQ entry
+
+`runtime_tick` takes an IRQ at the first instruction boundary after it is
+pending and unmasked. The entry writes the PC (the vector at `18h`, in the
+zero-wait BIOS) and costs the refill, 2 cycles plus the vector's N+S fetch
+waits, as mGBA's `ARMRaiseIRQ` charges `ARMWritePC`. When a DMA's stolen
+cycles were charged in the same tick, the refill is hidden: mGBA advances a
+CPU that a DMA blocks straight to its next event, and the refill passes
+within that wait. A wake from HALT adds `kIrqWakeDelayCycles` (7) before
+the entry.
+
